.TH NOIRE 1 "August 2026" "Noire 1.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noire \- control Noire through its GPUI interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noire
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B noire
opens the desktop control interface for the per-user Noire daemon.
With close-to-tray enabled, closing the window hides the controller and keeps
noise reduction running. Quitting Noire stops noise reduction before exit.
New daemon sessions start with noise reduction disabled unless the separate
startup option is explicitly enabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.TP
.BR \-\-minimized
Start with the window hidden in the system tray.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/noire/config.toml
Per-user configuration. The package manager does not create or remove this file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/noire/ui.toml
Desktop-only theme, start-minimized, and close-to-tray preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.rayan6ms.Noire.desktop
User-controlled login launcher created by the Start at login setting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR noirectl (1),
.BR noired (1)
